Z||000012||artherd||10-27-2001||03:26 AM||||I try to only power-brake at sanctioned burnought boxes at dragstrips  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>(actually, I don't do that there, I like to just go fast.)<P>sitting still while melting tyres dosen't appear to me, now lighting them up while I am MOVING....  well, that's what these cars were made for!!!<P>My goal is to make it as hard as possible (ie, real wheels/tyres) and still make expensive Pirelli smoke in third gear.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000013||rigdonhome||10-27-2001||09:28 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> Whoa!  Hey, jelly2m8, why don't you see if 'killjoy' is already taken as a username ???  You sound like the typical grumpy old man.  Do you really own a Fiero?  Why?<P>Abusing your car is part of the deal when you're a GearHead...  Why else would you own a high performance vehicle?  If you don't enjoy driving a car hard, buy one of those tire-smoking Geo 3-cyl grocery getters you're talking about.  Feed the pigeons in the park.  Play bingo with your buddies at the nursing home...<P>About the driveway...  It's a sad driveway that doesn't have at least one burnout on it!  If the road in front of your house is covered with your and your buddies' burnouts and donut marks, it's a sign that someone is actually ALIVE there!  Primped, perfectly cut, 'keep off the grass' lawns and spotless driveways are for the average, mundane suburbanite.  Luckily, fun-loving GearHeads aren't stifled by the anality it takes to stress about black marks on the driveway...<P>I've never heard a GearHead wonder/worry about how something broke on his/her vehicle.  More likely, you'll hear them say, "Cool.  Now I have an excuse to upgrade to stronger parts."  Stronger parts take more abuse.  More abuse equals more fun. <BR>The smell of tire smoke, gear lube, and gasoline are the ONLY smells that count when you're a GearHead.  I'll take a guess that your home and car both smell like daisy-fresh lysol!<P>I have, personally, smoked the tires in a 3-cyl Geo, and it was, in fact, Very Cool!!!  Burnouts are ALL cool, and the harder you have to work for it the cooler it is.  Burnouts are one of the founding principals of GearHeadHood, and if you don't understand why GearHeads like them, no one will ever be able to explain it to you.  I suppose you like to drive your high performance vehicle at the speed limit in the slow lane, and only take it out of the garage (or off its blocks) when the weather is perfect...<P>You've blasphemed one of the most basic and holy of all GearHead joys...  The burnout!  You should hang your head in shame!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P>And 'immortal', thanks for sharing the experience you and your Dad had with your Fiero.  Unfortunately, the rest of us have to buy our own Fieros and fix them when we break them...<BR><P>------------------<BR>Scott Rigdon<BR>1988 Fiero GT, Black, 5-speed<BR>38,000 Original Miles!<BR>Web Site:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/</A> <BR>Story of buying my Fiero:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm</A> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://24.249.68.73/cars/88_fiero_gt/rear_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||11
Z||000014||Sage||10-27-2001||09:43 AM||||It's fun at the strip in staging.  Can you say "burn out"?  Try a bleach burn out sometime if you like fumes!  Seriously though, you need to make some major mods to make that safe for your car.  Oh, and it wouldn't hurt to have a fat bank account and a good mechanic available too!<P>Fun is in the eyes of the abuser...er...beholder...perpetrator?<P>It's your car, have at it!  I would suggest a vacant lot over your driveway though, just to save your rep in the nieghborhood and your driveway!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Have a good one!||||reg||5
Z||000015||DR650SE||10-27-2001||07:52 PM||||I bought my cars,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I break my cars, <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>I pay for my car parts,:P<P>I fix my cars, <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"><P>I have lots of fun,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"><P>Dad stays out, <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_zz.gif"><P>Repeat as necessary.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"><P>Lighten up, damn people.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||6
Z||000016||Loki||10-27-2001||08:13 PM||||Does everyone have to FLAME everyone else on this forum? ****  people lighten the hell up. If you dont like it cool, no biggy, he enjoys it, dont berate (sp?) people just cause they like things you dont...<BR> Also rigdonhome, Jell HAS a fiero with a rompin V8, lay off it people, DAMN!!!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/fieroloki/loki_sig.gif">    <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/fieroloki/w4[1].gif"> <BR>ICQ# 16477998||||reg||1
Z||000017||SLYGUY||10-27-2001||08:46 PM||||I just think it is a terrible waste of a fine automobile. Fieros are wonderful cars, and even though I've only had two I would never subject them to that sort of abuse.<P>"I love my cars too much to let anything happen to my babies".<P>I think that there is a screw loose or something. Unfortunately it is not going to be found just on the car. <P>I think you would have every bit as much fun taking extra special care of your Fiero. There are many benefits to a two sided relationship with this car. You take extra care of the lil' gem and it rewards you by running extra smooth and economically. It will leave you stranded very seldomly if at all and you can tell all your buddies how much fun you are having owning the car without the cheers/jeers you might be getting when you walk them out to where the car is kept and they see all the burnout marks. <P>You don't actually expect that car to last or be able to sell it honestly if/when you ever decided to do that do you?<P>Sly<P>P.S. Start by treating your car in the manner illustrated below.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ViewImage.jpg"> ||||reg||8
Z||000018||Rex||10-27-2001||08:58 PM||||MMMMMMMMmmm bet ya could do a nice burnout<BR>in that soapy water. LOL||||reg||1
Z||000019||rigdonhome||10-27-2001||09:15 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Loki:<BR><B>...Also rigdonhome, Jell HAS a fiero with a rompin V8, lay off it people, DAMN!!!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Now I'm completely confused.  If Jell HAS a V8 Fiero, should I be able to assume from his flame above that he nas never done a smoky burnout with it?  That just doesn't make any sense.  It's like when I pull up next to a new 'Vette at a stoplight and he won't race my Fiero...  He would smoke me for sure, but doesn't seem to want to run the car hard...  Why buy a Corvette?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>In any case, I shouldn't get involved in the flames...  I just can't help myself sometimes.  I have the same problem with Milk Duds.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>Even in the flames, I'm grinning from ear to ear...  I don't take it personally or lose sleep over it.  I figure if you can't take it, don't dish it out.  <P>I'm rambling now...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_drunk.gif">  I think my point is, usually I'm poking fun at other flamers, but end up coming across as a flamer too.  My therapist says this may be due to all of my repressed rage.  Who knows...<BR><P>------------------<BR>Scott Rigdon<BR>1988 Fiero GT, Black, 5-speed<BR>38,000 Original Miles!<BR>Web Site:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/</A> <BR>Story of buying my Fiero:   <A HREF="http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.RigdonHome.com/cars/88_Fiero_GT/14_hours_in_a_fiero.htm</A> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://24.249.68.73/cars/88_fiero_gt/rear_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||1
