Z||000021||DR650SE||10-27-2001||11:48 PM||||Geez people, man.  Let me clear up some things.  First of all before i started the burn out i wet the ground on an area that gets very slick.  Second, SLYGUY I wash and wax my car once a week very faithfully.  I already know how to replace the transaxle.  I replaced the clutch with a kevlar racing clutch.  I pulled the engine and all out to work on it in the winter for fun.  Third,  What I mean by not letting anything happen to my babies, is not doing something like hitting a tree.  Fourth,  I never plan on selling my cars,  I would give them to my little brother.  I don't mean to be a a jerk or anything but the car is to have fun.  Yes I have fun pulling the engine and all.  I also have fun taking car of my cars.  They are in super clean condition.  PLease do jump to conclusions because I'm only 20.  Tha pisses a young person off so much when you make generalizations about them just because theier young.  I may be 20, but I pay for all my gas, insurance, car repairs, ect.  All I want is to have fun.  Lighten up.  Now go out and have fun in your fiero!!<P>                         DT<BR>P.S. Jelly, tell me honestly that you never did a smokey burnout.<P>------------------<BR>2 Black 86 SE's V-6 4-SPD||||reg||12
